{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795261317,"nonce":"o26SDfc9Jr29AvqKwBIAb0Y9rs0=","message":"Region zeroing is gone (d2904633). Recycled regions are no longer memset. Each small allocation clears its last 16 bytes and each medium allocation clears the slack past its request, which is what the pool does. The HostHeap contract now says the contents of an allocation are unspecified. The runtime already cannot rely on zeroed memory because its own pool does not provide it. Held and large blocks still come zeroed from calloc.\n\nChecks on the x86_64 NUC: clippy clean, the 7 Immix unit tests, the collector and host-heap tests, and the Lua conformance suite under Immix. The suite is 46 of 46. One earlier failure (official_complete, files.lua:762) came from launching the run with nohup, which makes SIGHUP ignored in child shells and breaks a test that kills a shell with SIGHUP. It fails the same way on the default pool and passes when launched with setsid. The Mac was not used for this round.\n\nOld Immix, new Immix and the pool, interleaved on a quiet NUC, median wall time:\n\n| Workload | Pool | Immix before | Immix after | After / pool |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| w_phase | 1.46 s | 2.58 s | 2.08 s | 1.42 (was 1.77) |\n| w_hold | 1.71 s | 2.47 s | 2.16 s | 1.26 (was 1.44) |\n| tok2 | 1.93 s | 2.54 s | 2.41 s | 1.25 (was 1.32) |\n| w_grow | 0.32 s | 0.40 s | 0.38 s | 1.19 (was 1.25) |\n| Lua binary_trees | 0.14 s | 0.19 s | 0.18 s | 1.29 (was 1.36) |\n| tokenize | 0.09 s | 0.11 s | 0.11 s | 1.22 (was 1.22) |\n\nPeak RSS is unchanged.\n\nStill open, in order of payoff: marking on large live sets (tok2 marks about 2.5 times slower than the pool because the start table is walked for every candidate word), then the allocation fast path (about 3.7 ns per allocation over the pool on w_phase: the call through the table, the thread-local region and the start-byte store).","files":null}]}